{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210692,"nonce":"C1kYiABuGbj08mJ7BrPbj6QxLKw=","title":"Per-frame List scratch buffer reads back a non-Num element after minor GC","message":"hatch nature-garden: ~20 individual Renderer3D.draw calls per frame crashed on the first frame with `Buffer.writeFloats: every element must be a number (index 0)` from the per-draw UBO upload. The scratch was a plain Wren List refilled every draw via appendMat4_ (clear + 32 adds). A collect_minor inside the allocator-heavy draw window left element 0 holding a non-Num Value that failed as_num() on the plugin's slow List walker (plugins/wlift_gpu/src/lib.rs Buffer.writeFloats).\n\nHatch side is worked around: _drawUboFloats became Float32Array (typed-array memcpy path, no validator). _sceneUboFloats, _matUboFloats, _shadowUboFloats and _shadowInstancedFloats are still Lists on the slow path and exposed to the same window.\n\nThe runtime bug is unresolved: a List element mutated per frame from tiered code loses its value across a minor GC. The 2026-06-05 barrier fixes (interpreter set_reg, JIT SubscriptSet on known List, list_sort / shuffle) landed after this and may have closed it. Verify by reverting the scratch to a List in a stress test (20+ draws per frame, 60 s) before closing.","files":null}]}